        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## About the data in this workbook\r\n\r\nFleet findings come from **Azure Resource Graph** (`queryType: 1`). **Runtime details**\r\nand the selected-app Resource Health view use read-only ARM calls for one app. No Log\r\nAnalytics workspace, diagnostic setting or Application Insights resource is\r\nrequired, so the workbook returns results immediately in any subscription.\r\n\r\n### Verified Resource Graph behaviour\r\n\r\nThese findings were measured against live Function App resources, not assumed\r\nfrom ARM template documentation:\r\n\r\n| Source | Availability in Resource Graph |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| `microsoft.web/sites` top-level `properties` | Richly populated - the basis of this workbook |\r\n| `properties.siteConfig.alwaysOn`, `.http20Enabled`, `.functionAppScaleLimit` | Populated in tested fixtures |\r\n| Runtime stack | Flex uses `functionAppConfig.runtime`; Linux/Windows stack field coverage varies. Use Runtime details when absent. |\r\n| `properties.siteConfig.minTlsVersion`, `.ftpsState`, `.cors`, `.healthCheckPath`, `.remoteDebuggingEnabled`, `.ipSecurityRestrictions` | Keys existed but values were null in the surveyed resources |\r\n| `microsoft.web/sites/config` | **Not indexed at all** (zero rows) |\r\n| `microsoft.insights/diagnosticsettings` | **Not indexed at all** (zero rows) |\r\n\r\nBecause detailed site configuration is not reliably populated in Resource Graph, this\r\nworkbook does **not** display TLS, FTPS, CORS, IP-restriction, remote-debugging or\r\nhealth-check columns. Showing them would produce a column reading \"Unknown\" for\r\nevery app. These controls need direct ARM or Azure Policy evidence; they are not\r\nassessed by the fleet grids. The runtime and health drill-downs need no collector.\r\n\r\n### How severity is calculated\r\n\r\nLinux Consumption retirement exposure dominates, because it is a hard deadline\r\nrather than a tunable setting:\r\n\r\n| Severity | Condition |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| Critical | On Linux Consumption **and** 3 or more other findings |\r\n| High | On Linux Consumption, or 5+ findings |\r\n| Medium | 2-4 findings |\r\n| Low | 1 finding |\r\n| No detected findings | No findings from the assessed fields; not a compliance or health certification |\r\n\r\n### Scope\r\n\r\nAzure Functions only. Logic Apps (Standard) carry `kind = 'functionapp,workflowapp'`\r\nand are explicitly excluded, as are plain App Service web apps.\r\n\r\n### Key retirement dates\r\n\r\n| Date | Event |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| 30 September 2026 | Apps on the end-of-life **v3 runtime** on Linux Consumption stop running |\r\n| 30 September 2028 | **Linux Consumption plan retires** |\r\n\r\nReferences:\r\n[Retirement notice](https://azure.microsoft.com/updates/?id=499451) |\r\n[Consumption plan (legacy)](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/consumption-plan) |\r\n[Flex Consumption plan](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/flex-consumption-plan) |\r\n[Migration guide](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/migration/migrate-plan-consumption-to-flex)"
            },
            "name": "aboutText"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### Support and feedback\r\n\r\nFound an issue, a false positive, or a missing check? Please get in touch - detail\r\nwhich tab and which Function App or plan is involved, and the fix will be turned\r\naround quickly.\r\n\r\n**Bulent Ozkir**\r\n[bulento@microsoft.com](mailto:bulento@microsoft.com) |\r\n[bulentozkir@hotmail.com](mailto:bulentozkir@hotmail.com)\r\n\r\n### License\r\n\r\nCopyright (c) 2026 Bulent Ozkir\r\n\r\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this\r\nsoftware and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal in the Software\r\nwithout restriction, including without limitation the rights to use, copy, modify,\r\nmerge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to\r\npermit persons to whom the Software is furnished to do so, subject to the following\r\nconditions:\r\n\r\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all copies\r\nor substantial portions of the Software.\r\n\r\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,\r\nINCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A\r\nPARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT\r\nHOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF\r\nCONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE\r\nOR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.",
